<title>USA: New York City $468 mln GO bonds restructured.</title>
<headline>New York City $468 mln GO bonds restructured.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc. restructured a $468 million New York City tax-exempt general obligation bond offering by not reoffering the 2017 maturity.</p>
<p>THE CITY OF NEW YORK</p>
<p>RE: $467,690,000*</p>
<p>GENERAL OBLIGATION BONDS</p>
<p>FISCAL 1998 SERIES A AND B</p>
<p>WE HAVE RECEIVED THE VERBAL AWARD</p>
<p>ALL RETAIL ORDERS THAT WERE ENTERED FOR THE 2017B MATURITY HAVE BEEN MOVED TO</p>
<p>THE 2016B MATURITY.</p>
